    "content": "Nick Reiner, the 32-year-old son of filmmaker Rob Reiner and photographer Michele Singer Reiner, pleaded not guilty on February 23, 2026, to the first-degree murder of his parents, who were found stabbed to death in their Brentwood home on December 14, 2025. Nick has a long history of drug addiction, was living with them at the time, and was taken into custody immediately following the deaths. Key Details About Nick Reiner: Legal Status: Nick is being held in custody without bail, charged with two counts of first-degree murder with special circumstances. He has a next court appearance scheduled for April 29, 2026. Background: Nick has publicly documented his long struggle with drug addiction, starting at age 15, and had extensive time in rehabilitation centers. Relationship with Father: Nick co-wrote the 2015 film Being Charlie, a semi-autobiographical project about his addiction struggles, which was directed by his father, Rob Reiner, and helped them grow closer. Mental Health: He was placed into a yearlong mental health conservatorship in 2020. Rob Reiner and Michele Singer Reiner were found with multiple stab wounds after an argument occurred at a Christmas party the night before their deaths, according to reports. Disclaimer: As of March 2026, Nick Reiner is accused, but not convicted, of these crimes.",
